WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:06.049
As you can see, there's quite a bit to go over with this course, so let's just jump straight in.

2
00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:09.550
So, Chaos vehicle features. What is a Chaos vehicle?

3
00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:19.769
So, the Chaos vehicles plugin is a lightweight system for performing vehicle physics simulations in UE5.

4
00:00:19.769 --> 00:00:24.989
And it's been built from the ground up and replaces the legacy UE4 system.

5
00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:31.989
Now this gives you increased reliability, so the system supports AsyncTick physics overview mode,

6
00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:35.990
which gives you more reliable simulations and more predictable results.

7
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:42.380
It has a similar setup as the legacy system, so a vehicle is still represented by a skeletal mesh

8
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.380
and one or more blueprints, one or more wheel blueprints, should I say,

9
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:53.880
making it easier for anyone familiar with the legacy system to switch to the new Chaos system.

10
00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.880
It still uses a physics asset to provide the appropriate collision geometry for a vehicle.

11
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:04.359
And there's increased flexibility with this as well, because a vehicle can now have any number of wheels,

12
00:01:04.359 --> 00:01:08.579
as well as any number of forward and reverse gears.

13
00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:14.579
It also has some more experimental features that can give you less of a realistic and more like an arcade-like feel.

14
00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:19.579
So, using direct controls for individual roll, pitch and yaw torque,

15
00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:23.579
you can really get something feeling really cool and not necessarily super realistic.

16
00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:31.159
Chaos vehicles also now features a modular system, which gives you real-time construction and destruction of your vehicles.

17
00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:38.159
Now this is only available when using this specific modular vehicle system, which we won't be taking a look at today,

18
00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:44.159
but we will take a quick look at the differences between the two systems so that you can see how each one is used.

19
00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:52.379
So both the Chaos vehicle system and the modular vehicle system have both been designed from the ground up

20
00:01:52.379 --> 00:01:56.379
and can exist in the same project together and be used in tandem.

21
00:01:56.379 --> 00:02:05.750
And the main differences between the two systems are the vehicle's composition and the simulation representation.

22
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.750
So what do I mean by that?

23
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:13.069
The standard vehicle system bases your vehicle on a skeletal mesh.

24
00:02:13.069 --> 00:02:19.069
And this skeletal mesh will contain all of the different parts of your vehicle, skinned to a skeleton hierarchy.

25
00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:26.069
And that's set up in such a way that everything moves in the correct way and pivots from the correct points based on the position of all these bones.

26
00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:32.620
It's also a fixed topology, so these meshes are fixed, you can't change them.

27
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:36.680
It uses the physics asset for the collision of the vehicle.

28
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:45.680
And any animation that happens on the vehicle is skeletal mesh animation, so it's the joints driving the movement of the mesh.

29
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:55.030
Compared to the modular system, where you're not using skeletal meshes, instead it's a hierarchy of geometry collection components.

30
00:02:55.030 --> 00:03:03.030
And this means that you can add or remove these different components at runtime, giving you the ability to construct or destructure a vehicle whenever you like.

31
00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:09.860
And each geometry component can have its own simulation component to drive its behavior at runtime.

32
00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.860
And this means that each part of the car can be doing different things at the same time.

33
00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:26.620
When it comes to the simulation representation, the standard vehicle system uses one component to drive the entire simulation, and it's the wheel controller for wheeled vehicle.

34
00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:35.139
Whereas the modular vehicle system is a collection of separate simulation components assigned to a simulation tree.

35
00:03:35.139 --> 00:03:43.389
Now these modules can operate independently of one another, and any of the simulation components can be added or removed at any point in time.

36
00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:47.389
Thus giving you the construction or destruction ability.

37
00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:54.379
But like I said, you can use these two systems in tandem within the same project.

38
00:03:54.379 --> 00:04:00.379
So if your vehicles have really varied requirements, you're not going to be forced to use just one of these systems.

39
00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:07.819
Because Chaos Vehicles is a plugin, the first thing you're going to need is to enable the plugin.

40
00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:17.720
We also need a skeletal mesh for our vehicle, and along with that we need a physics asset.

41
00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:23.259
Then we'll need one or more wheels blueprints for the front wheels and the back wheels.

42
00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:27.259
In our case we'll be setting one up for the front wheels and one for the back wheels.

43
00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:33.639
And then a vehicle blueprint, which is going to take all of this information and then translate it from...

44
00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:38.410
Which is going to combine all of this information into movement onto the car.

45
00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:44.569
And then an animation blueprint to determine what the car looks like when it's moving.

46
00:04:44.569 --> 00:04:48.110
And the last thing will be a float curve asset.

47
00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:51.110
And this is just going to represent the torque curve for the engine.

48
00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:59.110
So that when we hit the throttle or hit accelerate, the vehicle will accelerate in a manner of our choosing.
